course: dictionary
lesson: 4506
title: Hazard: danger and guessing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hazard is something that could hurt you or cause damage. Hazards are everywhere, so learning to spot them keeps you safe. «A loose eye or button on a soft toy is a choking hazard; an adult should sew it on or remove it.» The word choking tells you what the danger is: the button could get stuck in a child's throat.
explain: The same word can work as a verb, which is a doing word. «I can only hazard a guess, but I think it will rain.» Here hazard means to make a guess when you are not sure. The clue is the phrase «only», which tells you the speaker is not certain.
explain: Hazard words often come with a warning. «Warning signs on a bottle, like a hazard symbol, mean the product can harm you.» Harm means hurt, so a hazard symbol tells you to be careful. When you meet hazard, ask yourself: what could go wrong here?
fact: A hazard is something that could hurt you or cause damage: a danger.
fact: «A loose eye or button on a soft toy is a choking hazard.»
fact: Hazard signs and symbols, often yellow triangles, warn you of danger.
fact: «Hazard lights» on a car flash to warn other drivers.
fact: As a verb, to hazard a guess means to make a guess when you are not sure. This use is formal.
exercise: «A loose button on a soft toy is a choking hazard.» What is a hazard? | *Something that could hurt you | A soft toy for babies | A type of cake | A pretty decoration with no danger at all
exercise: Sam says, «I can't be sure, but I'll hazard a guess: it's Tuesday.» What does hazard a guess mean? | Write the answer in ink | Shout the answer loudly | *Make a guess when you are not sure | Know the answer for certain
exercise: «Warning signs on a bottle, like a hazard symbol, mean the product can harm you.» Find and copy one word that means hurt. | *harm | warning | symbol | bottle
test: Which of these is a safety hazard at home? | A clean, dry rug | *A wet floor in the kitchen | A book on a shelf | A cup of cold water
test: Why do hazard lights flash on a car? | *To warn other drivers | To light up the car park | To make the car look pretty | To keep the engine warm
exam: Which sentence uses hazard as a verb? | Put the warning sign near the hazard. | The hazard symbol is yellow. | *I can only hazard a guess, but I think it will rain. | There is a fire hazard in the kitchen.
